cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below. Everything it computes is SYNTHETIC, classical software simulation; it is not field evidence and makes no superiority claims."
title: "spark-membrane: a fail-closed console that orchestrates pinned OES repositories without merging them"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Brisson"
    given-names: "Jean-François"
    affiliation: "Spark AI NLP"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-9778-5374"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sparkainlp-x/spark-membrane"
url: "https://sparkainlp-x.github.io/spark-membrane/"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-05"
abstract: >-
  Offline, standard-library Python console that audits native 32-channel
  frames with a conjunction of pinned, independently tested checks (the
  normative OES-32 residual, the oes32_engine Profile A sidecar and the
  OES-Resilience weighted score), reports advisory baselines and engine
  disagreement, and adds one new component: a seeded, protocol-capped
  one-index explorer whose verdicts (REPAIRED_IN_SIM / LATCH_HELD) are
  SYNTHETIC. Runs are hash-chained and rendered as an evidence passport.
  Upstream repositories are pinned by commit SHA, not copied.
keywords:
  - fail-closed
  - audit
  - telemetry
  - synthetic data
  - reproducibility
  - research software
  - python
